    { math: '2 · Networks have shapes', note: 'Feedback loops stabilise; feed-forward loops filter noise; hubs coordinate. Biological networks share motifs with engineered circuits — evolution found the same designs.' },
    { math: '3 · Emergence is the point', note: 'Properties like robustness, oscillation and switching belong to the network, not to any gene. You cannot read them off the parts list — only from models and measurements of the whole.' },
